      "message": "feat(cl,app): unwind continuous C at clear links against the machine's stated C travel\n\nA C-stamped live-tool path states its spindle angle unwrapped, so the\nrings of a Rotary Contour wind past the shipped mill-turn's -360..360\nand the machine check refused them. cl::unwind_c shifts each stretch\nbetween clear links by whole turns into the stated travel, writing each\nrewind as the part-frame orbit it is (rapid chords at the link point,\nsplit to the op tolerance) so verify and the post see it; a stretch no\nrewind can fit refuses by name. rotary_gate runs it after stamp_c when\nthe machine's C states a travel.\n\nRefs #33\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
